WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.997
A chart is a visual argument about data.

00:00:02.997 --> 00:00:09.740
Bar charts compare categories, line charts commonly show ordered change, and scatter plots show pairs of numeric measurements.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:15.360
The choice of chart, scale, labels and units affects how a reader interprets the evidence.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:23.850
A bar or column chart is a suitable starting point because the class names are categories and marks are numeric.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:27.596
Use a clearly labeled score axis and an appropriate baseline.

00:00:27.596 --> 00:00:32.090
A connecting line could misleadingly imply a continuous trend between unrelated categories.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.415
What usually suits ordered change over time?

00:00:35.415 --> 00:00:40.730
A line chart can show an ordered time series when its axes and units are clear.
